# DevOps And Local Operations

## Environment And Secrets

- Use environment variables for all runtime configuration.
- Commit `.env.example` with placeholders only. Never commit `.env`, database dumps, backups, tokens, passwords, or real connection strings.
- Required settings include `DATABASE_URL`, `APP_SECRET_KEY`, `APP_BASE_URL`, `ADMIN_USERNAME`, `SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE`, `MCP_ENABLED`, and `LOG_LEVEL`.
- If first-run setup supports `ADMIN_INITIAL_PASSWORD`, it must be one-time use and never logged.

## Docker Compose

- Keep compose files under `deployment/`.
- Use `deployment/docker-compose.local.yml` for app plus local PostgreSQL.
- Use `deployment/docker-compose.app.yml` for app-only deployment against an external PostgreSQL URL.
- Build FastAPI images from an official Python base image and use exec-form commands.
- Do not run Docker with `sudo`.

## Migrations And Startup

- Run `alembic upgrade head` as an explicit documented step before app startup in deployment.
- Local development may provide a helper script, but it must make migration execution visible.
- Do not auto-drop, recreate, or truncate databases from container startup.
- A deployment is not verified until `/health` confirms database connectivity.

## GitHub Actions Workflow Safety

- Workflow YAML must be ASCII-only.
- Validate YAML syntax before pushing when workflows change.
- Keep workflows small: lint/test, Docker build, and mirror rules are separate concerns.
- Do not author workflows directly on `main` unless explicitly requested.
- Use concurrency for deploy or mirror workflows that can race.

## Mirror Rules Workflow

- This project mirrors `.cursor/rules/` to `spacemanspiff99/vibecoding` after rules changes land on `main`.
- The vibecoding path is `projects/issue-tracker/cursor-rules/`.
- The mirror is one-way from this project to vibecoding. Never edit mirrored rule content in vibecoding by hand.
- The GitHub secret must be named `VIBECODING_MIRROR_TOKEN` and scoped only to vibecoding contents read/write.

## Verification Commands

Use the relevant subset before completion:

```bash
python -m pytest tests/
alembic upgrade head
docker compose -f deployment/docker-compose.local.yml up --build
python -c "import yaml; yaml.safe_load(open('.github/workflows/mirror-rules.yml'))"
LC_ALL=C grep -RIn '[^ -~]' .cursor/rules .github/workflows documentation/standards
```

If a command cannot run because the project is not initialized yet, say so and verify the files that do exist.
